    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600246": {
      "title": "Academic Service Manager (Undergraduate Enrolment) (REG)",
      "description": "Job Description - Academic Service Manager (Undergraduate Enrolment) (REG)  (2600246) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Academic Service Manager (Undergraduate Enrolment) (REG)  (2600246) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . The Registry is a key central administrative unit of the University supporting it in providing quality higher education. We administer and deliver a broad range of student and academic services, such as admissions, registration, quality assurance, class scheduling, examinations, and graduation. The Registry is also responsible for maintaining student records and providing secretarial support to Senate and its committees, and are integral in the governing of academic regulations of the University. We provide aspiring candidates with ample staff development opportunities and a promising career in higher education. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Registry : Academic Service Manager (Undergraduate Enrolment) (REG) - ( 2600246 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Registry Closing Date : 18/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Registrar or his/her nominee. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Overseeing the day-to-day operation of the Undergraduate Enrollment Team of the Registry in administering course enrollment, student registration, government subsidy and related reporting, and tuition fees matters; Executing initiatives to streamline and improve work processes and operations through system enhancements and innovative solutions; Leading and providing professional student services in support of undergraduate studies, with a focus on improving service efficiency; Collaborating with academic units and external stakeholders to ensure alignment between enrolment processes and programme requirements; Managing communication strategies and channels to effectively disseminate enrolment-related information to students and other stakeholders; Contributing to the review and implementation of policies, regulations, and procedures to ensure compliance; Monitoring and analyzing enrollment trends and data to provide insights and recommendations for strategic planning and decision-making; Supervising team members and promotes collaboration and continuous improvement within team; Performing other duties as assigned to support the overall mission and goals of the Registry. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognized degree with at least 6 years’ relevant post-qualification administrative and supervisory experience; Excellent interpersonal and communication skills in both English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; Strong organizational and problem-solving skills; Demonstrated leadership abilities and strong analytical skills, with a track record of making sound decisions and driving process improvements; High level of attention to detail and accuracy in data handling; Proficiency in computer applications, possess strong system sense for operation streamlining; Ability to multitask and work under pressure; and Proven experience in project management will be advantageous. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in July 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260024H": {
      "title": "Public Affairs Manager (Branding and Marketing) (PAO) (260024H)",
      "description": "Job Description - Public Affairs Manager (Branding and Marketing) (PAO) (260024H) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Public Affairs Manager (Branding and Marketing) (PAO) (260024H) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Public Affairs Office : Public Affairs Manager (Branding and Marketing) (PAO) - ( 260024H ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Public Affairs Office Closing Date : Ongoing Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Public Affairs or his/her nominee(s), the appointee will be responsible for supporting the Public Affairs Office and its Marketing Team in the following key duties: Formulating and implementing marketing and brand-building strategies and plans that aligned with the University’s mission and support student recruitment; Planning and executing integrated marketing campaigns across online, social media and offline channels; Driving the development of creative concepts and marketing materials, from concept to roll-out; Overseeing social media content production, monitoring and optimisation to maximise the University’s marketing and branding impact; Coordinating video production to support branding, marketing and student recruitment; Planning, implementing, and evaluating student recruitment advertising, promotions and outreach activities targeting prospective students and other key stakeholders; Leveraging market research and analytics to generate insights and action plans; Managing and supervising the Information Centre; and Undertaking any other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Public Affairs or his/her nominee. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competencies : A recognised degree, preferably in marketing, business, journalism, communications, public relations or related disciplines; At least 8 years of relevant post-qualification experience with a proven track record focusing on branding and marketing; Demonstrated success in managing omni-channel strategies with measurable results; Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret complex data and translate insights into actionable strategies; Strong aesthetic judgement with the ability to assess and uphold visual quality for branding; Knowledge of tools and platforms such as Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta Ads, and other Martech solutions is an advantage; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; Strong PR sense and awareness of reputational risk and brand consideration; Mature, detail-oriented, self-motivated, with a proactive, can-do spirit; A good team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; Well-organised with strong multi-tasking and time management skills; Capable of managing projects independently while working under pressure and tight deadlines; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and interview. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in August 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600262": {
      "title": "Student Services Officer (SOL)",
      "description": "Job Description - Student Services Officer (SOL) (2600262) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Student Services Officer (SOL) (2600262) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Open Learning : Student Services Officer (SOL) - ( 2600262 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : School of Open Learning Closing Date : 15/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting in planning and executing comprehensive social media and digital marketing strategies, to maximize the awareness of the School and its programmes; Executing student recruitment activities by supporting school promotion activities, including roadshows, expos, and networking events to strengthen audience connection; Identifying new platforms, tools, partnerships, and market opportunities to enhance school visibility and student acquisition; Providing support to study programme administration, course registration , and p rocess various kinds of student academic consultation related change of study; Liaising with internal and external parties to ensure that the school activities, services and programmes pertaining to distance-learning and part-time students’ learning and support are effectively provided; and Performing any other duties as assigned. The appointee may be required to work occasionally outside normal office hours, including weekday evenings, Saturdays and Sundays. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree, preferably with 3 years post-qualification working experience in marketing or event management; Experience in a marketing agency or sales and marketing field is an advantage, a good understanding and network connection in the educational landscape will be a plus; Strong problem-solving skills, with a proactive approach in managing multiple priorities effectively and an ability to work independently under tight deadlines; A good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese and Putonghua; and Proficient PC skills, including MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and the use of AI tools. Applicants may provide any of their marketing campaign portfolios in the application. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement po sted in Aug 2026 nee d not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260025R": {
      "title": "Senior Student Affairs Manager (SAO) (260025R)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Student Affairs Manager (SAO) (260025R) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Student Affairs Manager (SAO) (260025R) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Student Affairs Office : Senior Student Affairs Manager (SAO) - ( 260025R ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Student Affairs Office Closing Date : 15/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Leading and developing a small team within the Student Affairs Office, fostering a collaborative, accountable and supportive work environment; Providing strategic leadership for the review, enhancement, implementation and evaluation of the whole-person development scheme and mental health campaign to strengthen their reach, effectiveness and responsiveness to students’ evolving needs; Overseeing the governance, development and effective management of student societies, including advising and developing student leaders, promoting responsible and inclusive participation, and ensuring compliance with relevant University policies and procedures; Building effective partnerships across the University and with external stakeholders to advance student-focused initiatives; Driving evidence-informed innovation and continuous improvement across student affairs programmes and practices, with clear objectives and measurable outcomes; Ensuring the effective planning and delivery of initiatives through sound project management, resource coordination, risk management and stakeholder communication; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Director of Student Affairs or his/her nominee(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree, preferably a higher degree, together with substantial administrative experience in tertiary education; Substantial experience in student affairs or a related field, with a proven track record of leading the development, enhancement, implementation and evaluation of student-focused programmes; A genuine commitment to whole-person development, student well-being and mental health promotion, with the ability to empower student leaders and foster an inclusive and vibrant student community; Excellent communication, interpersonal and people-management skills, with the ability to lead and motivate a team; Strong project management, stakeholder engagement and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and oversee the effective governance and development of student societies; Strategic thinking, sound judgement and a clear vision for enhancing the student experience, together with the flexibility to respond to evolving needs; and Proficiency in English and Chinese (including Putonghua) is required. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
