 Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office: Assistant Director of Information Technology (Management Information Systems) (ITO) - ( 26002BC ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 26/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Chief Information Officer, the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Leading the Management Information Systems team to plan, develop, enhance, and maintain management information systems for the University, such as Human Resources Management System, Financial Management Systems, Facility Management System, Customer Relationship Management System, Access Control System, and Information Enquiry and Broadcasting Systems; Developing, reviewing, and implementing policies and guidelines to provide quality application system services; Managing internal resources and external resources, such as vendors, to implement application system projects; Providing professional advice and support to users on application system implementation; Providing executive support to committees and working groups; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline; Substantial knowledge and experience in supporting Oracle e-Business Suite development platform and technical infrastructure, as well as hands-on experience in the implementation ERP systems and online self-services, preferably with managerial experience in tertiary institutions; Solid and extensive experience in web/application/database server administration and configuration is desirable; Profound leadership, independent and proactive with good analytical and problem-solving skills; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and proficient in both English & Chinese Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002BD": {
      "title": "Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO) (26002BD)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO)  (26002BD) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO)  (26002BD) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office: Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO) - ( 26002BD ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 26/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Chief Information Officer (Digitalisation and A.I.), the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing leadership for the planning, implementation and maintenance of the University’s AI Platforms and related services and applications; Overseeing AI system development, integration, data security and process automation to ensure efficient and effective operations across academic schools and administrative offices; Collaborating with stakeholders to analyse needs and translate them into system requirements that meet the current and future needs of the University; Organising AI training sessions and promoting AI tools/solutions to students, administrative staff, academic staff and researcher to support AI in teaching and learning, research, administrative operations; Supervising an information system team to develop, enhance and maintain University’s AI platforms, AI tools, AI-enabled applications and automation solutions; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science or Information Technology or related disciplines; Substantial knowledge and experience in designing, developing, integrating and supporting AI-enabled applications and automation solutions to enhance the new Student Administration System and other University operations and services; Experience in integrating AI platforms/tools, application APIs and internal/external systems to automate processes, improve service efficiency and support University operational needs; Hands-on experience in the implementing AI workflows, AI agent systems, admission/applicant websites and student self-service portal, preferably with managerial experience in tertiary institutions; Solid and extensive experience in cloud platform administration and configuration is desirable; Ability to evaluate and adopt emerging AI, agentic, cloud and application technologies to meet University initiatives; Proven ability to collaborate with other IT/IS teams, vendors, systems implementers and user departments; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and proficient in both English & Chinese. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260027I": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260027I)",
